WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.430
This is the Singularity Daily, for Thursday, October 29.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.480
Here are the last 24 hours in AI, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.690
Shields up. Google's strongest AI yet,

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.090
Gemini 4 Carbon, goes to cyber defenders first.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.730
It tops a major AI leaderboard, and it's scary good at finding security holes.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.150
With America's midterms next week,

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.430
OpenAI's opening an election war room, staffed in the hundreds.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.120
Ask ChatGPT for a fake photo of a long voting line?

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.020
You'll get a cartoon instead.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.880
In New York, chatbots can no longer pretend to be a kid's friend,

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.390
boyfriend or girlfriend.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.660
And Australia's lower house passed a bill banning

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.470
chatbots that foster emotional intimacy with kids.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.450
Now, the money. SK Hynix, which makes AI memory chips,

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:07.080
just had a $79 billion quarter.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.650
And OpenAI, one of Nvidia's biggest customers,

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.870
reportedly plans to buy Google's AI chips too.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.010
Bloomberg says Anthropic's picked JPMorgan to se

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.080
ll its IPO shares to everyday American investors.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.490
And someone's selling a used $60 million AI supercomputer on eBay.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:29.530
Free shipping, no returns.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.330
This week, Anthropic bought a one-person biotech that ran on Claude.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:37.190
Its treatment doubled grip strength in mice.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.600
And Formation Bio, an AI drug company, raised $600 million to buy stalled drugs.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.640
The catch? Musk's xAI offered to buy neighbours' homes,

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.500
if they drop their lawsuit.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.790
Anthropic found experts went along with their AI 86% of the time.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.760
Now, robots.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:08.300
South Korea's handing about 1,700 robots to government agencies next year.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.790
Unitree, the Chinese robot maker,

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:14.790
says sales jumped 70% last quarter, though profit fell.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.570
This week in China, 110 robots danced in sync. A world record.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:27.020
So, shields up. The smarter AI gets, the more it matters who gets it first.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.030
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.780
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.370
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.710
Want the whole month? Join Peter Xing live in Sydney tomorrow night.
